BREWMETRICS COFFEE CO.
BUSINESS INTELLIGENCE MINI PROJECT

1. PROJECT OVERVIEW

The BrewMetrics Coffee Co. Business Intelligence project focuses on developing an interactive Power BI solution for analysing coffee sales performance.

The project uses sales transaction data from April to June and provides insights into product trends, city-level performance, store-format performance, and sales growth.

The project is also maintained using GitHub and Power BI Project (.pbip) format so that changes to the BI solution can be tracked and reviewed through version control.

2. DATA MODEL

The Power BI solution uses a Star Schema consisting of a central fact table and multiple dimension tables.

Fact Table:

Fact_Sales
- Date
- City
- Store Format
- Item
- Quantity
- Unit Price
- Sales Amount

Dimension Tables:

Dim_Date
Used for date and time-based analysis.

Dim_City
Used for analysing sales performance across different cities.

Dim_Product
Used for analysing product-level sales performance.

Dim_StoreFormat
Used for comparing Flagship, Kiosk, and Drive-Thru stores.

The dimension tables are connected to the Fact_Sales table using one-to-many relationships.

3. DAX MEASURES

The following measures were developed for the Power BI solution:

- Total Sales
- Total Quantity
- MoM Growth %
- Running Total Sales
- City Sales Rank
- Average Sales per Transaction

These measures support sales growth analysis, cumulative sales analysis, city ranking, quantity analysis, and overall performance analysis.

4. DASHBOARD FEATURES

The Power BI dashboard provides interactive analysis of sales performance.

The dashboard includes:

- Total Sales summary
- Cold Brew sales trend
- City-level sales comparison
- Product-level sales analysis
- City slicer
- City to Store Format drill-down hierarchy

The drill-down feature allows users to move from overall city performance to individual store-format performance within each city.

5. KEY BUSINESS INSIGHTS

Insight 1: Cold Brew Seasonal Pattern

Cold Brew sales show a noticeable increase during April and May. This indicates a seasonal sales pattern for Cold Brew during the analysed period.

Insight 2: City-Level Performance

Bengaluru consistently records higher sales performance compared with the other cities in the dataset. The City Sales Rank measure and city-level visualisations make this difference easier to identify.

Insight 3: Store Format Analysis

The City to Store Format drill-down provides a more detailed view of sales performance by allowing users to analyse Flagship, Kiosk, and Drive-Thru stores within individual cities.

6. VERSION CONTROL

GitHub was used to maintain the Power BI project and its development history.

The project includes the Power BI Project file, report files, semantic model files, documentation, and supporting project files.

The commit history provides a record of changes made during the development of the BI solution.

7. TOOLS USED

- Microsoft Power BI Desktop
- Power BI Project (.pbip)
- Power Query
- DAX
- GitHub
- Visual Studio Code
- GitHub Copilot

8. CONCLUSION

The BrewMetrics Coffee Co. Business Intelligence solution demonstrates how Power BI can be used to transform sales transaction data into an interactive analytical dashboard.

The solution enables users to analyse sales trends, compare city performance, examine product patterns, and explore store-format performance.

Using GitHub and Power BI Project format also provides a structured and traceable development workflow for the BI solution.
